@7332. Would make truths serve evils of life.

@7355. "The servants and people of Pharaoh" = all things in the Natural. The things there which are inservient to confirm falsities are called "servants." @7357. (Compare @7396.) @7448. @7543. @7632.

@7562. "The servants of Pharaoh" = the things of the natural mind. @7563. @7565.

@7652. "The servants of Pharaoh" = those who infest of a lower sort. @7773, Explained. @7787. @8143.

@7819. He loves self as a means to the end that he may serve the Lord... and the world as a means that he may serve the neighbour.

@7934. "Ye shall keep this service" (Exodus 12:25) = worship on account of deliverance. @7936. @8057.

@7998. "Every man's servant" (verse 44) = man as yet natural.

@8049. "The house of servants" (Exodus 13:3) = spiritual captivity... For "service" = infestation by falsities. @8866, Explained.

@8168. To "serve the Egyptians" (Exodus 14:12) = to surrender themselves to those who infest. @8169.

@8241. "Moses His servant" (verse 31) = Divine truth ministering. Explained.

@8292. "I will divide the spoil" = slavery -servitium-. Explained. @8293.

@8313[4]. Those in charity want to serve all as the lowest; whereas those in faith (only)... want to be served by all.

@8553. In man, what ought to dominate is inservient; and what ought to serve, dominates.

@8866. It is slavery -servum- to be led by those in Hell. References.

@8873. "Thou shalt not serve them" (Exodus 20:5) = no Divine worship for them. To "serve" = submission... To "serve" (as distinguished from to "bow down to") = worship from the truth of faith.

@8890. "Thy man-servant" (verse 10) = the Natural as to truth. References.

@8906[end]. Truths and goods... then come into a state of slavery -statum servum-. Signified, Explained.

@8912. "A man-servant" = the affection of spiritual truth.

@8974. "When thou shalt buy a Hebrew servant" (Exodus 21:2) = those in the Church who are in truths of doctrine, and not in good according to them. Explained... "A servant" is predicated of those in truth and not in the corresponding good; and, in general, of truth relatively to good.

@--[2]. The reason these are represented by "servants," is that the things of the External Church are, relatively, nothing but services...

@--[3]. The reformation of such is treated of here in the laws concerning man-servants and maidservants.

@8975. "Six years shall he serve" (Exodus 21:2) = a state of labour and of some combat, and of the consequent confirmation of truth. @8981.

@8976. "In the seventh he shall go out free" (Exodus 21:2) = a state of confirmed truth. Explained.

@8977. "If he came in his body" (that is, a man-servant alone without a woman) (verse 3) = truth without delight... The men of the External Church, represented by the "Hebrew servants," are those who learn truth from no delight. Explained.

@--[3]. These are meant by those who want to serve for ever. Explained. (See also @8985-8991. @AE 208[13].)

@--[4]. These are the arcana in these statutes concerning servants. Explained.

@8979. "If he be lord of a woman" (Exodus 21:3) = truth conjoined with delight.

@--. "An (Israelitish) man-servant" = the man of the External Church, possessed of the truth of doctrine, but not the corresponding good; because he does truth and good (merely) to be rewarded. Explained.

@--[2]. Thus the man of the External Church is relatively a servant... and was represented by the servant called "a Hebrew servant," because he was bought from the sons of Israel.

@8980. "The man-servants," here, = (those) in a delight which counterfeits the corresponding good... Their "going out" from service (with their woman) = their state when received into Heaven; but as they are solely in faith... they are admitted no further than the entrance. Explained.

@8981. "If his lord shall give him a woman" (verse 4) = good adjoined to truth by the Spiritual, while in combat. Explained. (See also @8983-8991.)

@8988. Those who act solely from obedience... are relatively in servitude -servitute-. Explained.

@--[2]. But to serve the Lord by acting according to His precepts, and thus by obeying Him, is not to be a servant, but is to be free. Explained.

@8991. "He shall serve him for ever" (verse 6) = to obey to eternity... Such can never be brought to a state in which they act from good... They are perfected as to obedience; but do not attain to anything of charity. (See @3869[11].)

@8993[2]. For all that which derives its origin from the love of self, or the love of the world... is servile -servum-.

@8994[2]. Those in truth and not in the affection of it... are represented by "the man-servants from the sons of Israel."

@9034. "A man-servant" = scientific truth, which is the truth of the literal sense. Explained. (This "smitten." Explained.)

@9039[end]. (The Angels) place all glory and joy in serving; and, when in this state, they are in dominion. Explained.

@9058. "When a man shall smite the eye of his man-servant" (verse 26) = if the internal injures the truth of faith in the external man... "A man-servant" = scientific truth in the external man, thus also the external man. (See also @9060-9063.)

@9081. "A man-servant" = truth in the Natural. (This destroyed. Explained.)

@9093[2]. "No one can serve two lords"... = to serve the Lord by faith, and the world by love; thus to acknowledge truth, and do evil. ( = those called "Luke-warm." @9210[3]. @AE 233.) @AE 409[7]. @730[3], Explained.

@9096[end]. Slavery -servum- is to be led by cupidities which are from Hell. References.

@9180. Submission and service. Signified, Explained.

@--[end]. Good done for the sake of gain must serve.

@9318. To "serve" = obedience, and also worship. References.

@9322. To "serve" = worship. @9347.

@9449. Serving the neighbour for the sake of the neighbour (a sign that sins are remitted).

@9586. To do evil from delight is (really) slavery -servum-... "Everyone who does sin is the servant of sin." @NJHD 142. @AE 409[9].

@9776. "The service of the Habitation"... "Service" = the External or Natural of man, Explained.

@9806[4]. "Servant" is predicated from truths.

@9877[end]. Those not in this good of love... are in a state of slavery -statu servo-. Explained.

@10409. Slavery is to be led by self. @DP 44.

