@3417[2]. The delight of being of service to others; thus wanting to be "the least."

@3913[3]. By dignities (a spiritual man) can be of service to the neighbour...

@--[4]. When the things of the external man... are of service to the ends of the internal.

@3928. For the use of being inservient to heavenly delight.

@3951[end]. (Wealth, food, etc.) held as a means of subserving the end.

