Set.; Occidere.
Setting.; Occasus.
See <West>.

@AC 1837. "The sun was setting -ad occidendum-" (Genesis 15:12) = the state before consummation.

@--. The setting of the sun is the last time of the Church, called consummation.

@1859. "The sun had set" (verse 17) = the last time, when there is consummation. @AE 539[3].

@2353[2]. "The setting of the sun," etc. = falsities and evils.

@3693. "The sun had set" (Genesis 28:11) = life in what is obscure. Explained.

@--[2]. "The setting of the sun" = falsity and evil in which are those with whom there are no charity and faith; thus also the last time of the Church; and it also = what is obscure as to the things of good and truth... Illustrated.

@5097[2]. The Lord sets with everyone who does not receive truth and good. Not that the Sun there sets... but he who does not receive it causes it to as it were set with himself. (So the natural sun) does not set... Thus the setting -occiduum- is not in the sun.

@6693[5]. "The sun shall set at noon" (Amos 8:9) = that the good of celestial love would recede.

@8615. "Until the setting -occidere- of the sun" (Exodus 17:12) = when that state ceased. Explained.

@9031. The sun neither rises nor sets... (So) the Sun of Heaven is said to "set," when man is in evil and thence in falsity... The Lord is always in the rising... and never in the setting.

@9213. The "entering," or setting, "of the sun" = a state of shade from the delights of external loves.

@--. The setting of the Sun in Heaven corresponds to a state of shade as to the truths of faith, and to a state of cold as to the good of love...

@9653[2]. "Its setting" = good from Him in obscure perception.

@AE 179[10]. They sacrificed the Passover when the sun had set, because the setting of the sun = the last time of the Church.

@401[16]. "The setting of the sun" = the evil of love, which is the evil of life. Illustrated.

@--[28]. "The setting of the sun" also = the state of the Church when it is in ignorance, which is its first state. It also = the state of the Church when it is in evils and falsities. Illustrated.

@422[6]. "From the rising and from the setting" = all in the goods and truths of the Church. Illustrated.

@644[20]. "The setting" (Luke 12:54) = the end of the Church.

@721[7]. "Her sun has set while it is as yet day" (Jeremiah 15:9) = to perish as to all goods of love.

Set apart.; Dicare.

@AC 1909. Affections... dedicated to their uses.

@9296[2]. The understanding is set apart for the reception of truth; and the will is set apart for the reception of good. @9297[2].

Set apart.; Seponere.

@AC 9409. "The sons of Israel who were set apart" (Exodus 24:11). Explained. @9411[2].

Set before. See <Prefer>.

Set over. See <Govern-Praeficere>.

Set up. See <Statue>.

Seth.; Scheth.

@AC 335. "Seth" (Genesis 4:25) = a new faith given by the Lord through which charity was implanted. @436, Explained. @437. Explained. @439.

@462. The Second Church, which was not so celestial as the Most Ancient one, is called "Seth" (Genesis 5:2, 3).

@481. A new Church not very unlike the Most Ancient... called "Seth." Signified. @484.

@484[end]. The "likeness" of Seth was as a spiritual man of the "sixth day."

@485. The Church "Seth," here, is a different one from that described by "Seth" in Genesis 4:25. Explained.

@502. The three Churches, "Man," "Seth," and "Enos," constitute the Most Ancient, with a difference of perfection as to perceptions...

Settle. See <Certain>, and <Separate-Dirimere>.

Seven.; Septem.
Seventh.; Septimus.
Sevenfold.; Septempliciter. Septuplum.
Septenary.; Septenarius.
Seven-times.; Septies.
See <Sabbath>, and <Week>.

@AC 74. The celestial man is "the seventh day"... @84.

@84. Therefore the seventh day was sanctified.

@395. "Cain... avenged sevenfold" (Genesis 4:15) = that it would be sacrilege; for "seven" = what is sacred. @433.

@--. The septenary number was held sacred on account of... the "seventh day," which is the celestial man... Hence the septenary number so often occurs... and intervals of time were distinguished into sevens, and were called "weeks -septimanae-." Illustrated. @433.

@482. The septenary number, in the Word, everywhere = something holy or sacred as to the states which the times or other things involve.

@713. "Of every clean beast seven, seven -septena, septena-" (Genesis 7:2). Explained.

@716. "Seven -septena-" = holy things; for the Lord is the "seventh day," and, from Him, every celestial Church, or man, nay, the Celestial itself... Hence "seven," in the Word, = what is holy... @--[2], Illustrated.

@717. "Seven" is predicated of voluntary things.

@724. "Seven -septena-" = holy things; here, holy truths, which... come from goods.

@728. "In seven days" (verse 4) = the beginning of temptation... and also the end of vastation. @753. @1670.

@--. For "seven" is a holy number, and = the Lord's advent into the world, and His advent into glory; and every advent of His in particular. Explained, Illustrated.

@--[2]. The times are still more sacredly and certainly designated by (these) septenary numbers.

@--[3]. "Seven days" (Ezekiel 3:16) the beginning of visitation.

@--. "Seven months" (Ezekiel 39:12, 14) = the last limit of vastation, the first of visitation.

@--. "Seven times shall pass over him" (Daniel 4:32) = the end of vastation, and the beginning of a new man.

@--[end]. (Thus) "in seven days" = the beginning of a new Church, and the end of the old one.

@813[2]. "Seven," in the Word, = what is holy. @881. @900. @2832[7]. @2905. @3325[8]. @4670[end]. @5198.

@851[2]. The spiritual man (also) after temptations, becomes... not "the seventh day," like the celestial man, but "the seventh month." @852.

@889. "He waited yet other seven days" (Genesis 8:12) = the beginning of a third state. Explained.

@900[2]. See <Last Judgment>.

@1988. When "seven" occurs, instead of seven what is holy comes to the Angels; for "seven" = what is holy from the fact that the celestial man is "the seventh day," or Sabbath.

@2252[3]. Under <Fifty>, see this reference.

@2720[6]. Abraham's "seven ewe lambs" (Genesis 21:29) = the holiness of innocence.

@2723. Under <Beersheba>, see this reference.

@3824. "I will serve thee seven years" (Genesis 29:18) = study, and then a holy state. Explained. @3845.

@4123. "A way of seven days" (Genesis 31:23) = what is holy of truth.

@4347. "Seven times" (Genesis 33:3) = of the highest degree.

@5265. "Seven" = what is holy; and also involves a whole period from beginning to end. References. @6540.

@--[2]. That "seven" = holy things, is from the signification of numbers in the World of Spirits...

@--. "Seven," in the supreme sense, = the Divine itself; and, in the representative sense, the Celestial of love...

@5268. "Seven," in the opposite, = what is profane.

@--[2]. That "seven" = both holy and profane things. Illustrated.

@5339. "Seven years" (Genesis 41:47) = the first states. @5340.

@6775. "The seven daughters" (Exodus 2:16) = the holy things of that Church.

@7346. "Seven days" (Exodus 8:25) = an entire period from beginning to end; thus a full state.

@7885. "Seven days" (Exodus 12:15) = what is holy.

@7890. "Until the seventh day" (verse 15) = a full holy state. @8058. @8059.

@7892. "In the seventh day" (verse 16) = the end of the state.

@7905. "Seven days" (verse 19) = the entire period of this, state.

@8422[end]. Conjunction is signified by "the seventh day."

@8505[end]. Why no manna on the seventh day.

@8509. "On the seventh day" (Exodus 16:27) = a state of conjoined good and truth. @8507. See @8889.

@8889[end]. Hence "the seventh day" (Exodus 20:10) = a holy state.

@8893. "Rested on the seventh day" (verse 11) = then peace and the good of love. "The seventh day" = a state of celestial love; and thence what is holy, References. @8894.

@8976. "The seventh year" (Exodus 21:2) = a state of the conjunction of good and truth; (here) a state of confirmed truth. Explained.

@9141[4]. "Seven years" (Ezekiel 39:9) = a full state, thus to the full.

@9226. "Seven days" (Exodus 22:30) = the first state of those being regenerated; for "seven" = from beginning to end, thus what is full. @9228, Fully illustrated.

@9228. "The light of the sun sevenfold -septupla-, as the light of seven days" (Isaiah 30:26) = a full state of intelligence and wisdom from love and faith. @AE 257[6]. @401[10].

@9274. "In the seventh year thou shalt let the land rest" (Exodus 23:11) = the second state when man is in good. Explained.

@--[3]. This (second state of regeneration) is meant by "the seventh day," "the seventh year," and "the jubilee."

@9278[3]. "The seventh day" = that when man is in internals, then, being in Heaven with the Lord, labour and combat cease, and he is in the tranquillity of peace, in which also conjunction is effected.

@9279. "On the seventh day thou shalt cease [from work]" (verse 12) = a state of good when in internals, and the tranquillity of peace then. Explained.

@9288. "Seven days" (verse 15) = a holy state.

@9325[8]. To "bear seven" (1 Samuel 2:5) = to be regenerated to the full.

@9432. "In the seventh day" (Exodus 24:16) = when truth has been conjoined with good.

@9569. "Its seven lamps" (Exodus 25:37) = the holy spiritual things thence.

@10102. "Seven days" (Exodus 29:30) = a full state, thus what is plenary. @10120. @10127.

@10127. Both "seven," and "three" = what is full; but "seven" is said where holy things are treated of. @AR 505[2]. @AE 20.

@10367. "In the seventh day" (Exodus 31:15) = a state of good, which is the end -propter quem-.

@10374. "In the seventh day He rested and breathed" (verse 17) = a state of good when the Church has been instaurated, or when man has been regenerated; for "the seventh day" = a holy state... In the supreme sense, "the seventh day" = the union of the Divine Itself and the Divine Human... Hence "seven" = what is holy.

@10656. "Seven days" (Exodus 34:18) = a holy state from the appropriation of Divine truth... For "seven days" = a state holy from beginning to end.

@10730. "In the seventh day" (Exodus 35:2) = the second state of regeneration, when man has conjunction with the Lord; and, in the supreme sense, the union of the Human with the Divine Itself.

@AR 10. "The seven Churches" (Revelation 1:4) = all in the Christian world... for "seven" = all things and all persons; and, thence, what is full and perfect; and it is said in the Word where holy, or profane, things are being treated of; and therefore this number involves what is holy, or profane. Illustrated.

@14. "The seven Spirits" (verse 4) = all in Divine truth; in the abstract, Divine truth itself. @155.

@43. "Seven candlesticks" (verse 12) = the New Church. @AE 62.

@51. "Seven stars" (verse 16) = all Knowledges of good and truth. @155. @AE 184.

@237. "The seven lamps... are the seven Spirits of God" (Revelation 4:5) = the New Church... through the Divine Truth.

@257. "Seven seals" (Revelation 5:1) = completely hidden. "Seven" = all -omne-, thus completely. @AE 300.

@270. "Seven horns" (verse 6) = omnipotence. "Seven" = all. @AE 316.

@271. "Seven eyes" (Revelation 5:6) = omniscience. "Seven" = all, and is said of a holy Thing. @AE 317.

@390. "Seven Angels" (Revelation 8:2) = the universal Heaven. "Seven" = all, or all things; and thence the whole and universal. @657.

@472[3]. "Seven thunders" (Revelation 10:3) = (a full disclosing and manifestation); for "seven" = all, all things, and the whole.

@477. "The voice of the seventh Angel" (verse 7) = the final exploration and manifestation.

@516[end]. "Seven" = all and all things, and is predicated of the holy things of Heaven and the Church; and in the opposite, of these profaned.

@519. "The seventh Angel sounded" (Revelation 11:15) = the exploration and manifestation of the state of the Church after consummation, when there is the Lord's advent and Kingdom. Explained. @AE 681, Explained.

@538. "Seven heads" (Revelation 12:3) = insanity from truths falsified and profaned; for "seven" is predicated of profane things. @724. @737.

@TCR 301. The seventh day is for the Lord...

@302. "The seventh day" = man's conjunction with the Lord, and, thereby, regeneration.

@SE 5648. On the seven mountains of Babylonia. Explained.

@AE 20. "Seven," in the Word, = beginning and end, thus an entire period, and a full state; and therefore all, because all make what is full... and therefore where magnitude is treated of, "seven" = what is full; and where multitude, "seven" = all. @24. @62. @257, Illustrated.

@183. "The seven Spirits of God" (Revelation 3:1) = all the truths of Heaven and the Church. @274.

@256. "The seven Churches" = all who are of the Church; in the abstract, all things of the Church.

@257[4]. To "forgive seven-times" (Luke 17:4) = all times.

@--[9]. "Seven," and "seven times" = all things, and what is full. Illustrated.

@274. "The seven lamps" = all truth in the complex.

@314[10]. "Seven" = all -omne-, and what is full, and is predicated of what is holy 336. @602.

@357[end]. "Seven years" = all things, what is full, and altogether.

@401[19]. To "bear seven" = to be endowed with all the truths of the Church. @721[7].

@430[2]. There are simple numbers... 2, 3, 5, and 7; "7" = what is holy. @532.

@475[18]. "Seven times" (to wash) = what is plenary, and is predicated of holy things, such as Divine truths.

@486. "The seventh" = what is full and consummated, thus the last.

@489. "The seven Angels" = all the Heavens. @500.

@555[3]. "Seven (women)" = what is holy.

@684[36]. "Seven weeks" (Daniel 9:25) = a full time and state.

@700[16]. The priests being seven, their going round (Jericho) seven days, and seven times on the seventh day (Joshua 6) = what is holy, and the holy preaching of Divine truth; for "seven" (here) = what is holy on one side, and what is profane on the other.

@715. "Seven heads" = all knowledge of the holy things of the Word adulterated. @775.

@717. "Seven diadems" = all ultimate Divine truths profaned.

@717[13]. "Seven" is said of the holy things of the Word and of the Church.

@928. "Seven Angels having the seven last plagues" (Revelation 15:1) = all Divine truths from the Lord manifesting evils and falsities in the whole complex. @949.

@1062. "The seven heads are seven mountains" (Revelation 17:9) = (that the holy things of the Word profaned are the goods of the Word adulterated and profaned).

@1063. "And are seven kings" (verse 10) = the truths of the Word falsified and profaned.

@1067[2]. "Seven" = the truth of good profaned.

Seven Churches.; Septem Ecclesiae.

@AR 10. "John to the Seven Churches" (Revelation 1:4) = to all who are in the Christian world, where is the Word, and through it the Lord is known, and who accede to the Church... If these live according to the precepts of the Lord in the Word, they make the Church itself, ( = to all those who are in truths from good, or in faith from charity. @AE 20. @58. @92).

@40. "Send it to the Churches, those in Asia" (verse 11) = for those in the Christian world who are in the light of truth from the Word.

@43. "I saw seven golden candlesticks" = the New Church, which will be in illustration from the Word. "The seven candlesticks are the Seven Churches;" and by "the Seven Churches" are meant all who are in the Christian world, and accede to the Church. Explained.

@66. "The seven candlesticks which thou sawest are the Seven Churches" (verse 20) = the New Church on the earth, which is the New Jerusalem descending from the Lord out of the New Heaven... As "seven" = all, by "the seven candlesticks" are not meant Seven Churches, but the Church in the whole complex, which in itself is one, but is various according to reception. These varieties may be compared to the various jewels in a king's crown, and also to the various members and organs in a perfect body, which still make a one. The perfection of every form comes forth from varieties suitably placed in their order. Hence it is that the universal New Church with its varieties is described by "the Seven Churches" in what follows. ( = that all these are in the New Heaven and in the New Church. @AE 91).

@69. The Seven Churches are (here) treated of, by which are described all those who are in the Christian Church, who have religion, and from whom the New Church, which is the New Jerusalem, can be formed; and it is being formed from those who approach the Lord alone, and at the same time perform repentance from evil works. The rest... are indeed in the Church, but have not anything of the Church in them.

@73. By "the Seven Churches" are not meant Seven Churches, but the Church in the whole complex, which in itself is one, but is various according to reception... and it is hence that the universal New Church with its varieties, is described by "the Seven Churches" in what follows.

@87. "What the Spirit saith unto the Churches" (Revelation 2:7) = the things which the Divine truth of the Word teaches those who will be of the New Church, which is the New Jerusalem... As the universal Church is meant, it is not said, "what the Spirit saith to the Church," but to "the Churches."

@88. As in the things written to the Seven Churches is described the state of all in the Christian Church who can receive the doctrine of the New Jerusalem, and live according to it, thus who can be reformed through combats against evils and falsities, it is said to each, "He that overcometh."

@AE 62. "The Seven Churches" = all who are of the Lord's Church, thus the Church in general; and also Heaven, because Heaven and the Church make a one; moreover. Heaven is in those in whom is the Church. (Explained.)

Seventh.; Sevene.

@AE 654[39]. That falsities will destroy the understanding of truth, is signified by "from the tower of Seventh shall they fall in it by the sword" (Ezekiel 30:6).

@--[53]. "The land of Egypt a waste from the tower of Seventh to the border of Cush" (Ezekiel 29:10) = the destruction of the Church from primes to ultimates in the natural man.

Seventeen.; Septendecim.
Seventeenth.; Decimus septimus.

@AC 755. "The seventeenth day" (Genesis 7:11).

@--[2]. The number "seventeen" = both the beginning and the end of temptation, because it is composed of seven and ten. Explained, Illustrated.

@853. "The seventeenth day" (Genesis 8:4) = what is new.

@4670. "A son of seventeen years" (Genesis 37:2) = it state.

@--[3]. "Seventeen" = a beginning; here, the beginning of the representation by Joseph. It = a beginning and what is new; and moreover involves in general... all things represented by Joseph; for "seven" = what is holy; and "ten" = remains.

@6174. "Seventeen years" (Genesis 47:28) = the state there; for "seventeen" = from the beginning to the end, or from the beginning to what is new. Thus the seventeen years in which Jacob lived in Egypt = the beginning of the state of spiritual life in the Natural among scientifics even to its end.

Seventy.; Septuaginta.
Seventy times.; Septuagies.

@AC 433. "Seventy times" (Genesis 4:24) = what is much more a sacrilege.

@--[2]. The number seventy -septuagenarius-, which comprehends seven ages (derives its signification from seven), and when anything most holy, or most sacred, was to be expressed, it was said "seventy times seven"... which means to forgive as many times as he sins, so that it should be without end, or eternal, which is holy.

@--[end]. Thus "seventy times seven," here, = damnation.

@728[4]. The "seventy years" of the captivity = the (end of vastation and the beginning of a new man); for "seventy" and "seven" involve the same thing.

@1429. "Abraham was a son of five years and seventy years" (Genesis 12:4) = not so much of the Divine; "five" = little, and "seventy" = what is holy; here, being predicated of the Lord, "seventy" = the holy Divine.

@2906[5]. "Seventy years" (Isaiah 23:15, 17) = an entire period, from the time at which the Church began even till it expires. The "seventy years" of the captivity involves something similar.

@6024[end]. "Seventy" (Genesis 46:27) = what is full in order.

@6508. "Seventy days" (Genesis 1:3) = a full state; for "seventy" involves the like as "seven," which = an entire period from beginning to end, thus a full state; for multiplied numbers = the like as the simple ones of which they are composed.

@--[2]. That "seventy" = an entire period, thus a full state. Illustrated.

@--[3]. "Seventy years" (Jeremiah 25:11, 12; 29:10) = a full state of desolation and devastation: this was signified by "the seventy years" of the captivity.

@--[4]. "Seventy weeks" (Daniel 9:24) manifestly stands for a full state, thus for an entire period before the Lord would come; hence it is said that He came in the fulness of time. Explained.

@6642. "Seventy souls" (Exodus 1:5) = what is full.

@8369. "Seventy palm trees" (Exodus 15:27) = goods of truth in all abundance; "seventy" = all things in the complex, in like manner as "twelve."

@9228[end]. "Seventy" in like manner = what is full.

@9376. "Seventy of the elders of Israel" (Exodus 24:1) = the chief truths of the Church (all) concordant with good. "Seventy" = what is full, thus all things. ( = all who are in good from truths. @9404.)

@AE 684[34]. "Seventy weeks" = the time and state of the Church with the Jews down to its end; for "seven," and "seventy" = what is full from beginning to end.

Severe.; Austerus.

@CL 56[4]. Man (alone) is severe, etc.

@SE 1742. Tasted by the tongue as hard, soft, sour, sweet...

@5479[end]. Lagerberg was not a man for social intercourse, being austere.

Severely.; Severe.

@AE 827[2]. Severely prohibited.

Sew.; Assuere. Consuere.

@AC 216. To "sew a leaf" (Genesis 3:7) = to excuse.

@9212[7]. To sew or join the one to the other (Luke 5:36) is to destroy both.

Sex.; Sexus.
See <Love of the Sex>.

@AC 568[2]. See <Female>.

@CL 44[2]. There flashed from their eyes the fire of lust for the sex...

@--[3]. Cause that the companionships between the sexes - that is, between the youths and the maidens - are the heavenly sweetnesses themselves, which are pure.

@--[5]. With one of the sex. @--[6].

@55[5]. In cold towards their wives, and in heat towards the sex.

@--. They were then in a state of loathing for the sex.

@133. Without instruction man would not know how to discriminate sex, and nothing whatever about the ways of loving it.

@157. That in each sex there has been implanted from creation the faculty and inclination to be conjoined as into a one. Explained.

@223. This sphere is received by the female sex, and, through this, is transferred into the male sex. Explained.

@--. With the male sex there is no conjugial love, but it is solely with the female sex.

@--[end]. It is from the transference of this sphere from the female sex... that the mind is inflamed by mere thought about the sex.

@301. (By betrothing) the universal love towards the sex is determined to one man or one woman of the sex.

@304. Their souls separate themselves from the unlimited love of the sex...

@433[2]. Cold towards the sex (with confirmed adulterers), and at last loathing. @453. @505[end].

@508. This lust (of varieties) is love, and at the same time loathing, for the sex. Explained.

@TCR 585. In (plants) there are not two sexes; but every one is male.

@AE 555[13]. That the sexes are not to be confounded. Signified.

